---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import FunctionSchemaGenerator from '../../components/FunctionSchemaGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Function Calling Schema Generator" description="Generate a tool/function definition for Claude or OpenAI function calling from a simple parameter list.">
  <FunctionSchemaGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why clear schemas improve tool-calling accuracy</h2>
  <p>An AI model decides which tool to call and how to fill its parameters based entirely on the schema you provide — vague parameter names or missing descriptions lead to the model guessing incorrectly, while precise names and descriptions measurably improve correct tool selection.</p>

  <h2>How to use this generator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Name your function and describe what it does.</li>
    <li>List parameters with their types and descriptions.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated JSON schema into your API request's tools/functions array.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>A "get_weather" function with a required "location" string parameter generates a schema the model can use to correctly extract a location from user text and call the function with the right argument.</p>

  <h2>Common Function Schema Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vague parameter descriptions</strong> like "the input" instead of specific descriptions like "the city name, e.g. 'Paris, France'" — specificity directly improves the model's parameter-filling accuracy.</li>
    <li><strong>Not marking required parameters</strong>, causing the model to sometimes omit fields your function actually needs.</li>
    <li><strong>Overloading one function with too many responsibilities</strong> instead of splitting into focused, single-purpose tools the model can select between more easily.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Generate a Function Schema</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Defining a new tool for an AI agent to call</li>
    <li>Converting an existing API endpoint into an LLM-callable function definition</li>
    <li>Standardizing function schema format across a team building multiple tools</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Function Calling Schema FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Is the schema format the same across providers?</strong> Claude and OpenAI use very similar JSON Schema-based formats for function/tool definitions, with minor structural differences — check your specific provider's current documentation.</p>
</ToolLayout>
